<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<resources>
    <!--
        The colours in a values file, and none is for a screen. Every colour of a screen
        is a token in core/designsystem/theme/Color.kt; these are read by Android, outside
        Compose, where those tokens cannot be reached. Each repeats a colour of the theme, and a
        unit test fails if the two ever differ. The only other colour in XML is the white of the
        notification icon's and the car screen's icons (res/drawable/), which Android and the car
        replace with a colour of their own.

        The values are the brand's since 2026-10-13, when the app became Dually (ADR-010). The
        names kept their first word, "milo": a resource's name is the code's business, and no
        user sees it.
    -->
    <!--
        Android paints the window with it before Compose has drawn anything
        (res/values/themes.xml). The page colour of the theme; kept equal by
        WindowBackgroundTest.
    -->
    <color name="milo_window_background">#15120F</color>
    <!--
        The colour of the app's notifications (Notification.Builder.setColor): Android paints the
        small icon's surroundings with it in the notification shade, so the mark's orange shows
        where the icon itself cannot carry it (res/drawable/ic_stat_trip.xml). The accent of
        the theme; kept equal by NotificationAccentTest. Android may change it on a light or a
        dark shade so that the icon stays readable.
    -->
    <color name="milo_notification_accent">#FF5A12</color>
    <!--
        The Android Auto screen's colour (platform/car/TripStatusScreen.kt): the icons of its
        two rows and its button. The car draws the screen, outside Compose. The accent of the
        theme; kept equal by NotificationAccentTest. The car may replace it with a colour of its
        own where it judges the accent hard to read.
    -->
    <color name="milo_car_accent">#FF5A12</color>
    <!--
        The app's mark where Compose cannot draw it: the launcher icon's ground and its layer
        for themed icons (res/drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml and ic_launcher_monochrome.xml)
        and the widget's mark (res/drawable/widget_mark.xml). The orange square and the dark of the letter on it:
        the theme's pair for the mark, kept equal by AppMarkTest.
    -->
    <color name="milo_mark_ground">#FF5A12</color>
    <color name="milo_mark_letter">#1E1A17</color>
    <!--
        The face on the launcher icon (res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml, written by
        tools/make_launcher_icon.py from the brand design's "Icon A, Face"): the mascot's dials
        and his grin. The launcher draws it outside the app. These are the design's values for
        the drawing and belong to no screen; the line round the mouth is the mark's letter
        colour above. LauncherIconTest holds the drawing to these names.
    -->
    <color name="milo_icon_bezel">#E6E2DE</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_dial">#141210</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_dial_mark">#FFFFFF</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_redline">#FF3D2E</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_needle">#FF4A1C</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_mouth">#2A1712</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_tongue">#F2546B</color>
    <color name="milo_icon_teeth">#FFFFFF</color>
    <!--
        The home-screen widget's colours (res/layout/widget_home.xml): the home screen app draws
        it, outside Compose. Each is a colour of the theme, kept equal by WidgetColorsTest: the
        tile, the main and the secondary text, the accent, the text on the accent, and the fill
        of a quiet control.
    -->
    <color name="milo_widget_tile">#221D18</color>
    <color name="milo_widget_text">#FFF4E8</color>
    <color name="milo_widget_text_secondary">#CDBFAF</color>
    <color name="milo_widget_accent">#FF5A12</color>
    <color name="milo_widget_on_accent">#15120F</color>
    <color name="milo_widget_control">#2E2721</color>
</resources>
